### Tested versions

4.5-dev1

### System information

Depends on user

### Issue description

A few days ago I released an update to my game. In the update it replaces the old static Day sky with a new one that is animated using a sky shader.

To start, this is how the sky in my game is supposed to look. It looks like this on my own computer and works as intended. The system info string for my computer is:
Godot v4.5.dev unknown - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Single-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4050 Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6070) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-13500HX (20 threads)
![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/10721d86-de4e-4753-9085-ac33da2a7f50)


It works fine for other me, but other users have shown screenshots of the same sky being entirely black. I am pretty sure the screenshot below comes from a Window's user as well.
![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2748decd-0233-4c84-90cd-eb867b69f526)


On linux though, things seem to be completely different. Instead of the sky breaking by turning solid black, it gets full of various glitchy looking stuff.
The two screenshots below were taken by two different Linux users.
![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/221efa2c-473a-4bb4-a09c-f45d4adc70e2)
![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c730ccc1-a5df-4c82-9c2f-82fbaf05e84e)

### Steps to reproduce

To gather some information I made this program, which is included as the MRP. It has the intended sky shader on the left, the old static sky on the top right. The bottom 3 are variants of the top left sky with various elements removed to see if they cause it to display correctly.

Here is how it displays on my computer and this is how it is intended to display.
![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/93980830-22d4-4867-b9df-1559fad4692f)

I'm going to point out the difference between "Animated Sky" and "Animated Test", as that one has the smallest deviation yet in the received results it it isn't broken at all.


**Animated Sky**
```glsl
shader_type sky;
// Bopimo! Day Shader by FireCatMagic!

#include "../../PlaneTexture.gdshaderinc" // PlaneTexture.gdshader

group_uniforms Background;
uniform sampler2D background: source_color, repeat_disable;

group_uniforms Clouds;
uniform sampler2D clouds_top_above: source_color;
uniform sampler2D clouds_top: source_color;
uniform sampler2D clouds_bottom: source_color;

const lowp vec3 CLOUDS_MOVEMENT_SPEED = vec3(-1.75f, 0.0f, -1.75f);
const lowp float CLOUDS_TOP_ABOVE_SCALE = 230.0f;
const lowp float CLOUDS_TOP_SCALE = 150.0f;
const lowp float CLOUDS_BOTTOM_SCALE = 150.0f;
const lowp vec3 CLOUDS_TOP_ABOVE_POSITION = vec3(50.0f, 10.0f, 0.0f);
const lowp vec3 CLOUDS_TOP_POSITION = vec3(0.0f, 10.0f, 0.0f);
const lowp vec3 CLOUDS_BOTTOM_POSITION = vec3(0.0f, 10.0f, 0.0f);

group_uniforms Horizon;
uniform sampler2D horizon: source_color, repeat_disable;

void sky() {
	lowp vec3 background_texture = texture(background, SKY_COORDS).rgb;
	vec4 clouds_top_above_texture = plane_texture(clouds_top_above, CLOUDS_MOVEMENT_SPEED * TIME, CLOUDS_TOP_ABOVE_SCALE, true, vec3(EYEDIR.x, -EYEDIR.y, EYEDIR.z), CLOUDS_TOP_ABOVE_POSITION);
	COLOR = mix(background_texture, clouds_top_above_texture.rgb, clouds_top_above_texture.a);

	vec4 clouds_top_texture = plane_texture(clouds_top, CLOUDS_MOVEMENT_SPEED * TIME, CLOUDS_TOP_SCALE, true, vec3(EYEDIR.x, -EYEDIR.y, EYEDIR.z), CLOUDS_TOP_POSITION);
	COLOR = mix(COLOR, clouds_top_texture.rgb, clouds_top_texture.a);

	vec4 clouds_bottom_texture = plane_texture(clouds_bottom, CLOUDS_MOVEMENT_SPEED * TIME, CLOUDS_BOTTOM_SCALE, true, EYEDIR, CLOUDS_BOTTOM_POSITION);
	COLOR = mix(COLOR, clouds_bottom_texture.rgb, clouds_bottom_texture.a);

	lowp vec4 horizon_texture = texture(horizon, SKY_COORDS);
	COLOR = mix(COLOR, horizon_texture.rgb, horizon_texture.a);
}
```

```glsl
vec4 plane_texture(sampler2D plane_texture, vec3 plane_position, float scale, bool tiling, vec3 eye_dir, vec3 camera_position) {
	vec3 cam = camera_position - plane_position;
	vec2 euv = eye_dir.xz / abs( eye_dir.y );
	vec2 cuv = -cam.xz / cam.y;
	float cam_distance = length(cam);
	float absy = abs(normalize(cam).y);
	vec2 tuv = (euv-cuv) * cam_distance * absy / scale;
	if ( eye_dir.y < 0.0 && camera_position.y > plane_position.y )
	if ( tiling || max(abs(tuv.x),abs(tuv.y)) < 0.5 )
	return texture(plane_texture, tuv+vec2(0.5));
}
```


**Animated Test**
